* Silicon microring, part 2: self-pulsing just above the Hopf point and deep inside the window.
*
* Two rings as in ringchaos_bistable.net. Each laser is first raised past the up-jump fold (5 mW)
* to put its ring on the upper branch, then set to its final power:
*   X1: 0.40 mW, 7 % above the Hopf point (0.37328 mW): small, nearly sinusoidal pulsing;
*   X2: 6 mW: relaxation-like pulsing, the ring swinging on and off resonance.
* Reference: the same equations integrated with scipy (LSODA) in ringchaos_plots.py; the period
* and the extremes of the through power are compared.
* What to look for (measured at 2.16.2+6): X1 pulses at a 40.500 ns period (scipy 40.497 ns; the
* Hopf frequency, 24.7 MHz, is 40.4 ns), 0.0470-0.2054 mW; X2 at 96.174 ns (scipy 96.191 ns),
* 1.3268-5.9650 mW (scipy 1.3263-5.9650).
* Run: va-cli sim circuits/multiphysics/ringchaos_selfpulse.net --model models/multiphysics/ringchaos --tran --report o1,o2
VW wctl gnd DC 1550.155016
VP1 p1 gnd PWL(0 0 20n 5 2u 5 4u 0.40)
VP2 p2 gnd PWL(0 0 20n 6)
XL1 p1 wctl a0r a0i wl1 laser
X1 a0r a0i a1r a1i wl1 t1 siring
XD1 a1r a1i o1 detector
XL2 p2 wctl b0r b0i wl2 laser
X2 b0r b0i b1r b1i wl2 t2 siring
XD2 b1r b1i o2 detector
.tran 0.2n 20u
.end
